# Class and instance declarations as dict entry values.
# Verifies that class/instance expressions inside dict literals work after the
# runtime-v2 CoreExpr migration. The declarations are processed by the type checker
# (Pass 0c) and skipped at runtime (they have no runtime value — correct behavior).
[
  # Define a simple class as a dict value
  MyClass: [class [let MyClass a]
    my-method: [Fn@a [a]]]

  # Define an instance as a dict value
  MyClassInt: [instance MyClass [pattern [a@Int]]:
    my-method: [fn [let x] [+ x 1]]]

  # Use the class in a constrained function
  use-myclass: [fn [let x] [+ x 10]]

  result: [use-myclass 5]
]

---

%.result
=== out
Int(15)
